@inject TileArt Art

@* The match page's Help view: what doesn't need to be on the main screen every round (owner's choice, 24 Oct 2026).
   Your trait's goal, the tile types, the opening, a round, and scoring. *@

@{
    var match = Match;
    var me = match.Seats[You];
}
    <div class="match-help">
    <h2 class="h4">How to play</h2>

    @if (me.Trait is { } trait)
    {
        <h2 class="h4">Your trait: <span class="trait-name"><TraitIcon Trait="trait" /> @trait</span></h2>
        <p>@Capitalised(match.GoalText(trait).TrimEnd('.')). Everyone sees every trait from the first round.</p>
        <p>Your @(match.SpellsOf(me.Index).Count == 1 ? "spell" : "spells"): @string.Join(", ", match.SpellsOf(me.Index)).</p>
    }

    <h2 class="h4">Tiles</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        @foreach (var type in Enum.GetValues<TileType>())
        {
            <li>
                @if (Art.Paths is { } art && art.TryGetValue(type, out var image))
                {
                    <img class="tile-swatch" src="@Assets[image]" alt="" />
                }
                <span class="tile-mark">@Seats.Mark(type)</span>
                <b>@type</b>: @(type == TileType.Barren
                    ? "yields no mana. It turns up only in the later Unveils, never guarded, and still counts as land"
                    : match.Rules.Varies(type) ? $"rolls {match.Rules.YieldRange(type)} mana each round" : $"yields {match.Rules.YieldRange(type)} mana every round").
            </li>
        }
    </ul>
    <p><ManaIcon /> is mana. A held tile shows what it paid this round (<span class="text-nowrap">"+3 <ManaIcon />").</span> Monsters (☠) guard some tiles revealed later; beat them to take
        the tile.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">The opening</h2>
    <p>@match.Rules.OpeningUnveils drafts each reveal one tile per player, and everyone takes one in turn, for free. The
        first draft starts with seat 1, the next one seat later, and so on; the last to pick gets the tile left over.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">A round</h2>
    <p>Players pick stances in turn, one each, none twice in a round; the first picker moves one seat each round. When
        you pick a stance you take it first, @match.Rules.PickerDiscount mana cheaper; then every other player in turn may
        take it too, or pass. Each turn happens at once, for everyone to see.</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><b>Attune</b>: claim any free tile. Its price is your realm's base, plus 1 for each step beyond the first from
            your nearest tile, plus a die (1–@match.Rules.AttuneDieFaces). You see the price, then pay it or decline.</li>
        <li><b>Summon</b>: put Imps (power @match.Rules.ImpPower, @match.Rules.ImpCost mana) or Golems (power
            @match.Rules.GolemPower, @match.Rules.GolemCost mana, upkeep @match.Rules.GolemUpkeep) on one of your tiles.</li>
        <li><b>Attack</b>: send units at a rival's or a monster's tile next to them.</li>
        <li><b>Build</b>: an upgrade on one of your tiles.</li>
        <li><b>Cast</b>: your trait's spell (below).</li>
        <li><b>Channel</b>: gain @match.Rules.ChannelMana mana. Only its picker takes it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>With your own pick, units can also step between your neighbouring tiles first.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Spells</h2>
    <p>Each trait gives its player a spell (a Spellweaver gets them all). Ward, Blight, Lure and Pacify can go on
        several tiles in one Cast, each paid for. Pacified units can't attack for the rest of the round, even if they
        move; an attack that sends them goes without them.</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        @foreach (var s in GameRules.AllSpells)
        {
            <li><b>@s</b> (@match.SpellCostText(s)): @match.SpellEffect(s).</li>
        }
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h4">Scoring</h2>
    <p>Every round you bank points for your land and your mana income, and for tiles you take. At the end, upgrades and
        your trait's goal add theirs. After @match.Rules.Rounds rounds, the most points wins.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Every trait</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        @foreach (var t in Enum.GetValues<Trait>())
        {
            <li><span class="trait-name"><TraitIcon Trait="t" /> <b>@t</b></span> (@string.Join(", ", match.Rules.TraitSpells.GetValueOrDefault(t) ?? [])): @match.GoalText(t)</li>
        }
    </ul>
    </div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public Match Match { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter]
    public int You { get; set; }

    private static string Capitalised(string text) => text.Length == 0 ? text : char.ToUpperInvariant(text[0]) + text[1..];
}
